From 3103c3431b3690d140a0ec6a500954d4e39e1f36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:26:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 403/407] Unified: collisions through an assembly's motion,
 from the screen and the command line

The sweep turned named parts rigidly. DesignCheck.sweep_joint turns an
assembly's revolute joint step by step, solves it at each angle (the
parts move as the joints and formulas say: a cam's valve, a rocker) and
checks all the parts; pairs overlapping at every angle are told apart
(likely on purpose). The joint's angle is put back.

Screen: a revolute joint picked, the context bar's "Collisions" opens a
panel (from, to, step, stop); a hit turns the joint to its angle and
picks the two parts; a pair can be marked as overlapping on purpose.
Command line: --sweep with {"joint": name}.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
